---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="What I can help with · DuBose, M.D." active="help" bookbar={true}>

  <!-- 1 · Intro -->
  <section class="hero" style="padding-block:clamp(56px,8vw,88px)">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="page-head">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Scope of care</span>
          <h1>What I can help with</h1>
        </div>
        <p class="lede">
          We work on your health, not just your symptoms. Here is what
          that means in practice.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2 · What we work toward -->
  <section class="section band-tint">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">The goal</span>
        <h2>What we work toward</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Being my patient is an ongoing program for your health, built
          around what matters to you. Together we work to:
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="check-cols">
        <li>Help you feel better day to day</li>
        <li>Help you understand your health and your results</li>
        <li>Improve the numbers that matter, like blood pressure, weight, and labs</li>
        <li>Prevent disease where we can</li>
        <li>Keep existing conditions under control</li>
        <li>Improve sleep, fitness, and nutrition</li>
        <li>Catch problems early</li>
        <li>Keep screenings and vaccines up to date</li>
        <li>Help you stay independent and able</li>
        <li>Make progress on your own health goals</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="prose" style="margin-top:32px">
        We track these together, so we both know if care is working. I
        can&rsquo;t promise outcomes. I can promise we work on them and
        measure.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3 · Common situations -->
  <section class="section band-warm">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Where I&rsquo;m most useful</span>
        <h2>Common situations</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cards c2">
        <div class="card">
          <h4>&ldquo;It&rsquo;s several things at once.&rdquo;</h4>
          <p>
            Blood pressure, weight, sleep, stress. Each one manageable,
            together overwhelming. We sort out what&rsquo;s urgent, what
            matters most, and what can wait. Then we work through it in
            order.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h4>&ldquo;Something came back abnormal.&rdquo;</h4>
          <p>
            A lab result or scan with no explanation attached. I go
            through it with you: what it means, what to do next, and what
            to watch.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h4>&ldquo;My conditions deserve more than 15 minutes.&rdquo;</h4>
          <p>
            Diabetes, blood pressure, cholesterol, thyroid. Managed, not
            just refilled: medicines reviewed, complications watched for,
            numbers moving where we agreed they should.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h4>&ldquo;Nothing&rsquo;s wrong yet.&rdquo;</h4>
          <p>
            You want a doctor who knows your baseline, watches your
            trends, and keeps screening on schedule. Prevention works
            best before it&rsquo;s urgent.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card span">
          <h4>&ldquo;My health and my life are tangled together.&rdquo;</h4>
          <p>
            Stress affects sleep. Sleep affects eating. Money worry sits
            under it all, and your body keeps score. This is real
            medicine, and I take it seriously. We treat what needs
            treating and work the rest one realistic step at a time. When
            a counselor or financial professional is the right tool, I
            help you find one and stay involved.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4 · Conditions -->
  <section class="section" id="bookbar-after">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Day to day</span>
        <h2>Conditions I treat</h2>
        <p class="lede">Membership covers the full range of adult primary care.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="steps c3">
        <div class="step-item">
          <h4>Ongoing conditions</h4>
          <p>High blood pressure, diabetes and prediabetes, cholesterol,
          thyroid, asthma, acid reflux, gout, migraine, and more.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <h4>When you&rsquo;re sick</h4>
          <p>Infections, colds that won&rsquo;t quit, UTIs, rashes,
          stomach trouble, and injuries that don&rsquo;t need an ER.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <h4>Prevention &amp; screening</h4>
          <p>Annual reviews, cancer screening on schedule, vaccines
          planned, risk assessment.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <h4>Medicines</h4>
          <p>Reviewed as a whole: what&rsquo;s working, what&rsquo;s
          redundant, what&rsquo;s interacting. Refills handled
          promptly.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <h4>Mind &amp; mood</h4>
          <p>Depression, anxiety, adult ADHD, stress, burnout, and
          insomnia. Treated within primary care, referred wisely when
          needed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <h4>Lifestyle &amp; habits</h4>
          <p>Sleep, weight (including modern weight-loss medicines where
          appropriate), exercise, nutrition, alcohol, and tobacco.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="prose" style="margin-top:36px">
        Plus: labs and imaging ordered and explained, referrals with a
        real handoff, and the paperwork of being a patient included:
        disability and FMLA forms, letters, prior authorizations.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5 · What I don't do -->
  <section class="section band-warm">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Boundaries</span>
          <h2>What I don&rsquo;t do</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
        <div class="rows" style="margin-top:0">
        <div class="row">
          <b>Emergencies</b>
          <p>Chest pain, stroke signs, severe injury: that is 911 and the
          ER, always. Afterward, I help you make sense of what happened.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Hospital care</b>
          <p>The hospital&rsquo;s doctors run the admission. I stay
          informed and manage your care when you&rsquo;re home.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Specialist-led conditions, alone</b>
          <p>Some conditions need an oncologist or cardiologist leading.
          I refer well, co-manage, and keep the whole picture.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Mental health beyond my safe scope</b>
          <p>Serious psychiatric illness and addiction care beyond
          primary care get honest triage and a warm handoff.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Children</b>
          <p>Adults only (18+).</p>
        </div>
      </div>
        <p class="prose" style="margin-top:28px">
          If I&rsquo;m ever not the right doctor for something, I&rsquo;ll
          tell you directly.
        </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 6 · CTA -->
  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="inner">
        <h2>Not sure if your situation fits?</h2>
        <p>
          That is what the free conversation is for. Tell me what&rsquo;s
          going on, and I&rsquo;ll tell you honestly if I can help.
        </p>
        <a class="btn btn-inverse" href="/book">Book a free conversation</a>
        <p style="margin-top:22px"><a class="quiet" href="/how-it-works">How the membership works &rarr;</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
